     3,
     "<div><blockquote type=\"cite\">\r\n            <p style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\">Hi Dr van Hees and fellow GGIRers, </p><p style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\"><br></p><p style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\">Hoping someone can help here.  <span style=\"font-size:11pt\">I have used GeneActiv watches and GGIR to process my data.  My watches were all set to start recording at my local time which is timezone of Australia/Melbourne, usually start recording at 00:00hour.  </span></p><p style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><br></span></p><p style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\">1. Timezone issue: Out of 65 participants, I had 13 files which had time stamp errors.</span></p><p style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\"> </p><ul style=\"margin:0cm 0px;color:rgb(33,33,33);font-family:Calibri;font-size:16px\" type=\"disc\"><li style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">In GGIR csv file, the recording timestamps are correct, e.g., start recording at \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<p>2021-11-17 00:00:00:500.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"margin:0cm 0px;color:rgb(33,33,33);font-family:Calibri;font-size:16px\" type=\"disc\"><li style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">In GGIR csv file, I notice the start time is set wrongly to: Start Time 2010-09-16 09:10:00:000</li></ul><ul style=\"margin:0cm 0px;color:rgb(33,33,33);font-family:Calibri;font-size:16px\" type=\"disc\"><li style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">When data was processed in GGIR using the BIN files only, I get the following output.  The date and time are wrong as they reflect the start time as per CSV file instead of when the movement recording start. See image 1 below titled &quot;Wrong tz&quot;.</li></ul><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0cm 36pt;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\"> </p><ul style=\"margin:0cm 0px;color:rgb(33,33,33);font-family:Calibri;font-size:16px\" type=\"disc\"><li style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">I had previously been able to use desiredtz=”USA/ Hawaii” in GGIR (<u><span style=\"color:red\">version 2.6.0, ran on Windows</span></u>) to change the output to this, which appears correct according to my record.  See image below titled &quot;Corrected by desiredtz&quot;.</li></ul><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0cm 36pt;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\"><br></p><ul style=\"margin:0cm 0px;color:rgb(33,33,33);font-family:Calibri;font-size:16px\" type=\"disc\"><li style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">However, I tried to rerun the same file using the same desiredtz = “America/Hawaii” in GGIR (<u><span style=\"color:red\">version 2.9.0, on Mac</span></u>), I received an output where the timezone error was not corrected and it was as if the desiredtz code had no effect.  I ran my files with and without the timezone correction and both times it gave me the same results. I am wondering if there a specific way to ensure desiredtz is used in version 2.9.0?</li></ul><p style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\"> </p><p style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\">2. Guider = Sleeplog with no sleep log provided.  <span style=\"font-size:11pt\">When I went back to rerun the same analysis in PC using version 2.6.0, but this time without sleep log, the output in Part 4 stated Guider = Sleeplog instead of HDCZA.  </span></p><p style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><br></span></p><p style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\">Please advise how I can get desiredtz to work in GGIR version 2.9.0 and how to ensure the default HDCZA algothrim is used. </span></p><p style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"> </span></p><p style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\">I attach my GGIR script below for your reference.  </p><p style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\"><br></p><p style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\">g.shell.GGIR(</p><p style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\">  mode=c(1,2,3,4,5),</p><p style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\">  datadir=&quot;C:/Input_Files&quot;,</p><p style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\">  outputdir=&quot;C:/Output_Files&quot;,</p><p style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\">  do.report=c(2,4,5),</p><p style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\">  desiredtz=”USA/ Hawaii”,</p><p style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\">  #=====================</p><p style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\">  # Part 2</p><p style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\">  #=====================</p><p style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\">  strategy = 1,</p><p style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\">  hrs.del.start = 0,          hrs.del.end = 0,</p><p style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\">  maxdur = 18,                 includedaycrit = 16,</p><p style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\">  qwindow=c(0,24),</p><p style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\">  mvpathreshold =c(100),</p><p style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\">  bout.metric = 4,</p><p style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\">  excludefirstlast = FALSE,</p><p style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\">  includenightcrit = 16,</p><p style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\">  overwrite = TRUE,</p><p style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\">  </p><p style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\">  #=====================</p><p style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\">  # Part 3 + 4</p><p style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\">  #=====================</p><p style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\">  def.noc.sleep = 1,</p><p style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\">  outliers.only = TRUE,</p><p style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\">  criterror = 4,</p><p style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\">  do.visual = TRUE,</p><p style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\">  </p><p style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\">  #=====================</p><p style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\">  # Part 5</p><p style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\">  #=====================</p><p style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\">  threshold.lig = 30, threshold.mod = 100,  threshold.vig = 400,</p><p style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\">  boutcriter = 0.8,      <a href=\"http://boutcriter.in\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://boutcriter.in&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792489778349000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1gfPO1M-iDLBmpaeX_dCXW\">boutcriter.in</a> = 0.9,     boutcriter.lig = 0.8,</p><p style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\">  boutcriter.mvpa = 0.8, <a href=\"http://boutdur.in\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://boutdur.in&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792489778349000&amp;usg=AOvVaw077afT3XZCziGvEi96VQGZ\">boutdur.in</a> = c(1,10,30), boutdur.lig = c(1,10),</p><p style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\">  boutdur.mvpa = c(1),</p><p style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\">  includedaycrit.part5 = 2/3,</p><p style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\">  #=====================</p><p style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\">  # Visual report</p><p style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\">  #=====================</p><p style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\">  timewindow = c(&quot;WW&quot;),</p><p style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\">  visualreport=TRUE)</p><p style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\"> </p><p style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\">Thank you, all!</p><p style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\"><br></p><p style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\">Cheers,</p><p style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\">Susie</p>\r\n\r\n<p></p></blockquote></div>"
    ],
