    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"auto\" class=\"gmail_attr\">On Friday, May 19, 2023 at 6:28:29 PM UTC+10 Vincent van Hees wrote:<br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\">Hi Susie,</div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\"><br>Can you be more specific:</div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\"><br></div><blockquote style=\"border-left:3px solid rgb(200,200,200);border-top-color:rgb(200,200,200);border-right-color:rgb(200,200,200);border-bottom-color:rgb(200,200,200);padding-left:10px;color:rgb(102,102,102)\"><div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:rgb(33,33,33);font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;font-size:14.6667px;text-align:left;display:inline!important\">In GGIR csv file,<span> </span></span><br></div></blockquote><div><span style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);font-weight:400\">which GGIR csv file? GGIR outputs the time stamp in several csv reports. Knowing in which one of them the timestamp is not as expected can help to identify the problem.</span><span style=\"text-align:left;display:inline!important\"><span><br></span></span></div><div><br></div><div><span style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);font-weight:400\">Between release 2.7-0 en 2.8-0 some specific bugs were fixed in handling the timezone in sleep diaries when working on OSx and most problematic in timezones in the far east (Australia and eastward) as it undermined recognising the date correctly.</span></div><div><br></div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\">Regarding both questions. Could you share a test example to help me investigate the issue? I would need:</div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\"><ul><li><span>Raw file</span></li><li><span>Corresponding sleep diary line.<br></span></li></ul></div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\"><br></div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\">I do not have a OSx but can test it in Windows/Linux.</div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\"><br></div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\">Best,</div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\"><br></div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\">Vincent</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\">\r\n    <div>\r\n        </div></div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\"><br></div><div>\r\n        ------- Original Message -------</div><div><br>\r\n        On Wednesday, May 10th, 2023 at 12:43 PM, <a rel=\"nofollow\">susie...@gmail.com</a> &lt;<a rel=\"nofollow\">susie...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:<br><br>\r\n        </div><div><blockquote type=\"cite\">\r\n            <p style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\">Hi Dr van Hees and fellow GGIRers, </p><p style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\"><br></p><p style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\">Hoping someone can help here.  <span style=\"font-size:11pt\">I have used GeneActiv watches and GGIR to process my data.  My watches were all set to start recording at my local time which is timezone of Australia/Melbourne, usually start recording at 00:00hour.  </span></p><p style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><br></span></p><p style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\">1. Timezone issue: Out of 65 participants, I had 13 files which had time stamp errors.</span></p><p style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\"> </p><ul style=\"margin:0cm 0px;color:rgb(33,33,33);font-family:Calibri;font-size:16px\" type=\"disc\"><li style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">In GGIR csv file, the recording timestamps are correct, e.g., start recording at \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<p>2021-11-17 00:00:00:500.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"margin:0cm 0px;color:rgb(33,33,33);font-family:Calibri;font-size:16px\" type=\"disc\"><li style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">In GGIR csv file, I notice the start time is set wrongly to: Start Time 2010-09-16 09:10:00:000</li></ul><ul style=\"margin:0cm 0px;color:rgb(33,33,33);font-family:Calibri;font-size:16px\" type=\"disc\"><li style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">When data was processed in GGIR using the BIN files only, I get the following output.  The date and time are wrong as they reflect the start time as per CSV file instead of when the movement recording start. See image 1 below titled &quot;Wrong tz&quot;.</li></ul><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0cm 36pt;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\"> </p><ul style=\"margin:0cm 0px;color:rgb(33,33,33);font-family:Calibri;font-size:16px\" type=\"disc\"><li style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">I had previously been able to use desiredtz=”USA/ Hawaii” in GGIR (<u><span style=\"color:red\">version 2.6.0, ran on Windows</span></u>) to change the output to this, which appears correct according to my record.  See image below titled &quot;Corrected by desiredtz&quot;.</li></ul><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0cm 36pt;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\"><br></p><ul style=\"margin:0cm 0px;color:rgb(33,33,33);font-family:Calibri;font-size:16px\" type=\"disc\"><li style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">However, I tried to rerun the same file using the same desiredtz = “America/Hawaii” in GGIR (<u><span style=\"color:red\">version 2.9.0, on Mac</span></u>), I received an output where the timezone error was not corrected and it was as if the desiredtz code had no effect.  I ran my files with and without the timezone correction and both times it gave me the same results. I am wondering if there a specific way to ensure desiredtz is used in version 2.9.0?</li></ul><p style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\"> </p><p style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\">2. Guider = Sleeplog with no sleep log provided.  <span style=\"font-size:11pt\">When I went back to rerun the same analysis in PC using version 2.6.0, but this time without sleep log, the output in Part 4 stated Guider = Sleeplog instead of HDCZA.  </span></p><p style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><br></span></p><p style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\">Please advise how I can get desiredtz to work in GGIR version 2.9.0 and how to ensure the default HDCZA algothrim is used. </span></p><p style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"> </span></p><p style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\">I attach my GGIR script below for your reference.  </p><p style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\"><br></p><p style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\">g.shell.GGIR(</p><p style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\">  mode=c(1,2,3,4,5),</p><p style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\">  datadir=&quot;C:/Input_Files&quot;,</p><p style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\">  outputdir=&quot;C:/Output_Files&quot;,</p><p style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\">  do.report=c(2,4,5),</p><p style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\">  desiredtz=”USA/ Hawaii”,</p><p style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\">  #=====================</p><p style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\">  # Part 2</p><p style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\">  #=====================</p><p style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\">  strategy = 1,</p><p style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\">  hrs.del.start = 0,          hrs.del.end = 0,</p><p style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\">  maxdur = 18,                 includedaycrit = 16,</p><p style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\">  qwindow=c(0,24),</p><p style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\">  mvpathreshold =c(100),</p><p style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\">  bout.metric = 4,</p><p style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\">  excludefirstlast = FALSE,</p><p style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\">  includenightcrit = 16,</p><p style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\">  overwrite = TRUE,</p><p style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\">  </p><p style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\">  #=====================</p><p style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\">  # Part 3 + 4</p><p style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\">  #=====================</p><p style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\">  def.noc.sleep = 1,</p><p style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\">  outliers.only = TRUE,</p><p style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\">  criterror = 4,</p><p style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\">  do.visual = TRUE,</p><p style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\">  </p><p style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\">  #=====================</p><p style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\">  # Part 5</p><p style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\">  #=====================</p><p style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\">  threshold.lig = 30, threshold.mod = 100,  threshold.vig = 400,</p><p style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\">  boutcriter = 0.8,      <a href=\"http://boutcriter.in\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://boutcriter.in&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792489778356000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2KVfo-2Iqat_WrDhPlj1ya\">boutcriter.in</a> = 0.9,     boutcriter.lig = 0.8,</p><p style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\">  boutcriter.mvpa = 0.8, <a href=\"http://boutdur.in\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://boutdur.in&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792489778356000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1G4_7Ea4I3_YZkgS9P5GJa\">boutdur.in</a> = c(1,10,30), boutdur.lig = c(1,10),</p><p style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\">  boutdur.mvpa = c(1),</p><p style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\">  includedaycrit.part5 = 2/3,</p><p style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\">  #=====================</p><p style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\">  # Visual report</p><p style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\">  #=====================</p><p style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\">  timewindow = c(&quot;WW&quot;),</p><p style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\">  visualreport=TRUE)</p><p style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\"> </p><p style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\">Thank you, all!</p><p style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\"><br></p><p style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\">Cheers,</p><p style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\">Susie</p>\r\n\r\n<p></p></blockquote></div><div><blockquote type=\"cite\">\r\n\r\n-- <br>\r\nYou received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;R package GGIR&quot; group.<br>\r\nTo unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send an email to <a rel=\"noreferrer nofollow noopener\">RpackageGGIR...@googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\nTo view this discussion on the web, visit <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/RpackageGGIR/8f265987-a14f-4799-b54a-bb9280fbd4dbn%40googlegroups.com?utm_medium=email&amp;utm_source=footer\" rel=\"noreferrer nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/RpackageGGIR/8f265987-a14f-4799-b54a-bb9280fbd4dbn%2540googlegroups.com?utm_medium%3Demail%26utm_source%3Dfooter&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792489778356000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2HwdK2O6DStwVcpflBM9QF\">https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/RpackageGGIR/8f265987-a14f-4799-b54a-bb9280fbd4dbn%40googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\n\r\n        </blockquote><br>\r\n    </div></blockquote></div>"
    ]
   ]
  }
